    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I think that this model is a two-dimensional item response model with appropriate recoding of the missing item responses. It should work well with mirt::mirt.</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>Am Dienstag, 16. Februar 2016 04:57:14 UTC+1 schrieb Seongho Bae:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi, Phil.<div><br></div><div>Can I try 2PLM-NIMD in mirt()?</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\">Holman, R., &amp; Glas, C. A. (2005). Modelling non‐ignorable missing‐data mechanisms with item response theory models. </span><i style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\">British Journal of Mathematical and Statistical Psychology</i><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\">, </span><i style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\">58</i><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\">(1), 1-17.</span><br></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\">If can I, How it works?</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\">Seongho</span></div></div></blockquote></div>"
