  {
   "id": "9HQelUDXDAAJ",
   "from": "Seongho Bae",
   "author": "6a75f6f91a59c568",
   "date": "2016-02-22T11:30:06Z",
   "subject": "Re: Can I try 2PLM-NIMD? (* for Non Ignorable Missing Data)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello, Robi@ipn,<div><br></div><div>That is not two-dimensional item response model. One is response variables, another is the design matrix what indicate where NA values included. Within Two-dimensional models, all variables are &#39;response variables&#39;, not &#39;design matrix&#39; indicates which one is null.</div><div><br></div><div>See this if you available;</div><div><a href=\"http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/j.2044-8317.2005.tb00312.x/epdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/j.2044-8317.2005.tb00312.x/epdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475216887000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3U1kZsZTPeudd6EpDF9ydA\">http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/j.2044-8317.2005.tb00312.x/epdf</a></div><div><a href=\"https://www.ets.org/Media/Research/pdf/RR-10-11.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.ets.org/Media/Research/pdf/RR-10-11.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475216887000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3_h-rSf6LLr5kpNVPX6hi9\">https://www.ets.org/Media/Research/pdf/RR-10-11.pdf</a></div><div><br></div><div>Seongho<br><br>2016년 2월 16일 화요일 오후 7시 12분 35초 UTC+9, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">robi...@ipn.uni-kiel.de</a> 님의 말:</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I think that this model is a two-dimensional item response model with appropriate recoding of the missing item responses. It should work well with mirt::mirt.<br><br>Am Dienstag, 16. Februar 2016 04:57:14 UTC+1 schrieb Seongho Bae:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi, Phil.<div><br></div><div>Can I try 2PLM-NIMD in mirt()?</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\">Holman, R., &amp; Glas, C. A. (2005). Modelling non‐ignorable missing‐data mechanisms with item response theory models. </span><i style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\">British Journal of Mathematical and Statistical Psychology</i><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\">, </span><i style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\">58</i><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\">(1), 1-17.</span><br></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\">If can I, How it works?</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\">Seongho</span></div></div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div>"
