   "subject": "Re: Can I try 2PLM-NIMD? (* for Non Ignorable Missing Data)",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>Am Montag, 22. Februar 2016 12:30:06 UTC+1 schrieb Seongho Bae:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello, Robi@ipn,<div><br></div><div>That is not two-dimensional item response model. One is response variables, another is the design matrix what indicate where NA values included. Within Two-dimensional models, all variables are &#39;response variables&#39;, not &#39;design matrix&#39; indicates which one is null.</div><div><br></div><div>See this if you available;</div><div><a href=\"http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/j.2044-8317.2005.tb00312.x/epdf\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/j.2044-8317.2005.tb00312.x/epdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475216890000&amp;usg=AOvVaw05nAshgERu-QkVcwCI9-K2\">http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/j.2044-8317.2005.tb00312.x/epdf</a></div><div><a href=\"https://www.ets.org/Media/Research/pdf/RR-10-11.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.ets.org/Media/Research/pdf/RR-10-11.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792475216890000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ytYLGWHhBSHmtfXt2dvzD\">https://www.ets.org/Media/Research/pdf/RR-10-11.pdf</a></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>I think this is a two-dimensional model with original item responses (othe original items) and response indicators. The models specified in Rose et al. (2010) can be estimated with standard multidimensional IRT models. The first dimension refers to &quot;competency&quot; and the second to &quot;response propensity&quot;.<br><br>Alexander<br><br><br> </div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div>Seongho<br><br>2016년 2월 16일 화요일 오후 7시 12분 35초 UTC+9, <a rel=\"nofollow\">robi...@ipn.uni-kiel.de</a> 님의 말:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I think that this model is a two-dimensional item response model with appropriate recoding of the missing item responses. It should work well with mirt::mirt.<br><br>Am Dienstag, 16. Februar 2016 04:57:14 UTC+1 schrieb Seongho Bae:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi, Phil.<div><br></div><div>Can I try 2PLM-NIMD in mirt()?</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\">Holman, R., &amp; Glas, C. A. (2005). Modelling non‐ignorable missing‐data mechanisms with item response theory models. </span><i style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\">British Journal of Mathematical and Statistical Psychology</i><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\">, </span><i style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\">58</i><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\">(1), 1-17.</span><br></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\">If can I, How it works?</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:16.12px\">Seongho</span></div></div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div>"
